James inquired about how countries can adapt to climate change risks originating from their trading partners. I provided a detailed response outlining nine strategies: diversifying trade partners and goods, developing local supply chains, establishing international agreements, investing in resilient infrastructure, emphasizing a robust economy, ongoing risk assessment, utilizing technology, and focusing on training and capacity building. Each strategy is aimed at enhancing resilience against climate-related disruptions in trade, with an emphasis on collaboration and innovation tailored to each country’s specific economic and political context.
